<title>USA: InPhyNet-MedPartners merger terms adjusted.</title>
<headline>InPhyNet-MedPartners merger terms adjusted.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>MedPartners Inc and InPhyNet Medical Management Inc have adjusted the terms of their merger so that each InPhyNet share will be exchanged for 1.18 MedPartners shares, MedPartners said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Previously, each InPhyNet shares was to be swapped for 1.311 MedPartners shares.  </p>
<p>MedPartners said the adjustment resulted from discussions with the Securities and Exchange Commission that led to a restatement of InPhyNet's earnings for 1996 and for the 1997 first quarter.  </p>
<p>According to MedPartners, InPhynet restated its 1996 full-year earnings to $0.81 a share from $1.04. First quarter 1997 earnings were restated to $0.20 a share from $0.30.</p>
</text>
